the biggest active wildfire in the u.s  is tearing through drought-stricken  forests in new mexico threatening homes  and forcing thousands of residents to  flee for their lives  by nine o'clock 9 30  the smoke in the valley was so thick he  needed a butter knife to cut through it  so it was it came on really fast  at that point that's when the  law enforcement came up  to tell us to get out  the fires are visible from outer space  firefighters are dropping flame  retardant from helicopters and building  fire breaks with bulldozers  a high school gym has been set up as an  evacuation center  the fire has burned for nearly a month  destroying 300 houses and other  structures  dozens of small towns have been  evacuated in the rugged sangre de cristo  mountains  some residents in las vegas new mexico  east of santa fe have decided to stay  and fight the flames themselves this is  my home  i gotta predict it  i went down my property you know the  hose  the weather forecast doesn't hold out  much hope there's some bad winds coming  up  wednesday night  thursday really really strong  so it was uh if they don't contain it by  wednesday  we're going to be in real trouble  large new fires also broke out in  arizona and several other states  according to u.s agencies wildfires have  burned more than twice as much land this  year as in the same period of 2021  rob reynolds al jazeera
 

